    >>> jnp.put(x, indices, values, inplace=False, mode='clip')
    Array([10,  0, 20,  0, 30], dtype=int32)

    Alternatively, they can be wrapped to the beginning of the array:

    >>> jnp.put(x, indices, values, inplace=False, mode='wrap')
